{"id":"2f6dfa86-0ef9-4d6a-9e6e-e548e939e308","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The method parameter 'args' is never set within the method, so it remains as passed. The program point is at method exit, so this must remain true unless the method changes it.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.308544Z"}
{"id":"9750dba9-89a4-4141-8a66-15e9c92fab4c","expr":"b == null || b.doubleValue() != 0.0 || result == null","rationale":"If b is not null and its double value is zero, the result is null to indicate division by zero.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.309229Z"}
{"id":"3072e392-6985-4c14-8845-3369cb521af1","expr":"a != null","rationale":"The method uses a methods and instanceof checks, so a should be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.308655Z"}
{"id":"3f0976b2-f069-48aa-9008-743b18214bd6","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The main method is always invoked by the JVM with a non-null args array.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.308721Z"}
{"id":"4d080a21-f8cb-4679-b554-a2aa8fa2d080","expr":"b != null","rationale":"The method calls b.doubleValue() and b.intValue(); b must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.308655Z"}
{"id":"2f408d23-0ce6-4064-bb96-559e5e0cb51b","expr":"result == null || a != null","rationale":"A returned non-null result implies that a must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.309229Z"}
{"id":"95a0d437-eb91-4850-85f9-a320a5de2673","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"In Java, array length is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.308544Z"}
{"id":"13b3e94c-72e6-46c3-b3f9-abbe6af31bfb","expr":"result == null || b != null","rationale":"A returned non-null result implies that b must not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.309229Z"}
{"id":"6549a02b-f145-4e0f-9108-c223d9380f67","expr":"a.getClass().equals(b.getClass())","rationale":"The operation uses methods like intValue or doubleValue on both; inconsistent types may not be handled.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#safeDivide(T,T):T","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.308655Z"}
{"id":"fa9772d5-f0bc-4462-af03-036840b0ac56","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"Array lengths in Java are always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc2#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc2.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:12.308721Z"}
